<h2>What's Included</h2>

<p>Based on Akkio's published product descriptions, enterprise plans include access to:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Audience Agent</strong>: AI-powered audience building, segmentation, and lookalike modeling</li>
<li><strong>Strategy Agent</strong>: Media strategy recommendations, scenario modeling, and channel allocation</li>
<li><strong>Reporting Agent</strong>: Automated performance reporting, insight generation, and anomaly detection</li>
<li><strong>Predictive Analytics</strong>: Propensity modeling and forecasting across audience segments</li>
<li><strong>Integrations</strong>: Connections to media buying platforms, data warehouses, and agency data sources</li>
</ul>

<p>Feature access by tier is not publicly disclosed. The scope of what's included depends on the contract negotiated with Akkio sales.</p>

<h2>Typical Total Cost of Ownership</h2>

<p>For mid-size to large agency teams, the following cost factors apply beyond headline subscription fees:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Named user seats</strong>: Enterprise contracts cap user counts; additional users incur incremental costs. Clarify how seats are counted (named users vs. concurrent users).</li>
<li><strong>Onboarding and setup</strong>: Custom integration with agency data systems typically involves professional services. Confirm whether onboarding is included in the contract price.</li>
<li><strong>Annual commitment</strong>: Enterprise SaaS at this tier typically requires annual contracts. Month-to-month is unlikely to be available.</li>
<li><strong>Data integration fees</strong>: Connecting to proprietary agency data, third-party research platforms, or ad serving systems may carry additional costs.</li>
<li><strong>Training</strong>: Initial analyst training is a soft cost to factor in — ask what Akkio provides versus what you need to source independently.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who It's Best For / Not For</h2>

<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Mid-to-large agencies with dedicated analytics teams that need to scale audience building and media planning automation. Especially relevant for agencies aligned with Havas and Horizon Media network relationships or those evaluating AI-native planning tools.</p>

<p><strong>Not ideal for:</strong> Small agencies with limited analytics budgets or teams without technical resources to manage integrations. If your total annual budget for tools is under $50K, lighter-weight alternatives like Obviously AI or Google Cloud AutoML may be a better fit.</p>

<p>G2 rating: <strong>4.5/5</strong> from 14 reviews (<a href="https://www.g2.com/products/akkio/reviews">G2 — Akkio Reviews</a>)</p>

<h2>How to Negotiate</h2>

<ol>
<li><strong>Request a scoped proof-of-concept</strong> — Akkio's AI agents are best evaluated on actual agency data; a POC on a real campaign brief gives you leverage before signing an annual contract</li>
<li><strong>Benchmark against Pecan AI and Obviously AI</strong> — Both are direct competitors in predictive analytics; competitive quotes create pricing pressure</li>
<li><strong>Ask about network-level pricing</strong> — Holding company agencies with multiple offices or brand teams can often negotiate platform-wide rates</li>
<li><strong>Clarify integration costs before signing</strong> — Custom data connections can significantly increase total cost of ownership beyond the subscription fee</li>
</ol>

