<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>Does Akkio publish pricing?</h3>
<p>No. Akkio does not currently publish pricing on its website. All plans are custom-quoted through their sales team. Historical self-serve pricing of ~$49–$60/user/month has been reported on G2 but appears to no longer be available.</p>

<h3>What is the minimum budget for Akkio?</h3>
<p>No public minimum is stated. Given Akkio's positioning with large holding company agencies (Havas, Horizon Media), enterprise contracts are likely in the $50,000+/year range for meaningful team access. Confirm directly with sales.</p>

<h3>Is Akkio suitable for small agencies?</h3>
<p>Akkio is primarily designed for mid-to-large agencies with established analytics workflows. Small agencies with limited data infrastructure may find the platform over-built for their needs and should evaluate lighter alternatives like Obviously AI or Google Cloud AutoML first.</p>

<h3>How does Akkio compare to Pecan AI on price?</h3>
<p>Both use custom enterprise pricing and neither publishes list prices. Pecan AI emphasizes SQL-based data science workflows; Akkio emphasizes multi-agent media planning automation. Getting quotes from both vendors during evaluation is recommended for direct price comparison.</p>

<h3>What contract length does Akkio require?</h3>
<p>Enterprise SaaS platforms at Akkio's tier typically require annual contracts. Month-to-month terms may be available for pilot engagements but are not standard. Confirm with Akkio sales during the evaluation process.</p>

<h3>Does Akkio offer a free trial?</h3>
<p>Not indicated on their current public website. Contact Akkio through their website to request a demo or proof-of-concept engagement before committing to a contract.</p>

